<article class="case-feature"><figure class="case-art"><img src="/assets/images/work/teleme.png" alt="Screens from the Teleme mobile app" width="461" height="895" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><figcaption>Teleme · Work completed with the Upstack Studio team</figcaption></figure><div class="case-story"><p class="eyebrow">A closer look / Teleme</p><h3>Connecting people with doctors, from home.</h3><dl><div><dt>The need</dt><dd>A way for people to speak with a doctor without having to leave home.</dd></div><div><dt>The product</dt><dd>A mobile app connecting patients and doctors through video calls and messaging. Our team worked from prototyping through launch.</dd></div><div><dt>The lesson I take forward</dt><dd>Start with the person who needs help. The technology has to serve that need, not become the point of the project.</dd></div></dl><blockquote><p>“The end product is not only good but better than what we have expected.”</p><footer><img src="/assets/images/work/kevin.png" alt="" width="150" height="150" loading="lazy"><span>Kevin Ong<br>Former CTO, Teleme</span></footer></blockquote><p class="case-disclosure">Client feedback from the original project. This is past software work, not a result from the current AI Audit.</p></div></article>
